From 61be013b49544dfdbf932a50d2d642e1d8e7f031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <dev@phlink.invalid>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 03:14:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: vendor adblock-rust 0.12.2 via gnrt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Imports the `adblock` crate (Brave, MPL-2.0) plus 30 transitive
dependencies into //third_party/rust via the standard chromium_crates_io
+ gnrt workflow.

  vpython3 tools/crates/run_gnrt.py add adblock
  vpython3 tools/crates/run_gnrt.py vendor
  vpython3 tools/crates/run_gnrt.py gen

Two upstream license-file lookups needed manual help (gnrt couldn't
auto-detect them):
  * seahash-4.1.0 (MIT) — added LICENSE-MIT alongside the vendored
    crate and pointed gnrt_config.toml at it.
  * flatbuffers-25.12.19 (Apache-2.0) — copied LICENSE from a
    sibling Apache-licensed crate and pointed gnrt_config.toml at it.

The adblock target //third_party/rust/adblock/v0_12:lib is not yet
reachable from the GN graph (cargo_crate targets only materialize when
a consumer references them); standalone build verification is therefore
deferred to phase 5 plan 5-02 which adds the C++ wrapper at
//chrome/browser/phlink/adblock that links the rlib.

phlink PRD §5 (Adblock); phase 5 plan 5-01.
